* TuxSpice model cards for common bipolar transistors that LTspice's standard.bjt lacks.
* Written for TuxSpice: Gummel-Poon parameters fitted to datasheet typical values
* (hFE at the test current, VBE(on), fT -> TF, Cob/Cib -> CJC/CJE). They are
* approximations, not manufacturer models. Vceo, Icrating and mfg are picker metadata,
* as in standard.bjt. tests/test_models.py checks each one's hFE and VBE in ngspice.
.model BC337 NPN(IS=4E-14 BF=250 VAF=80 IKF=0.6 ISE=1E-14 NE=1.5 BR=10 RB=5 RC=0.3 RE=0.1 CJE=30E-12 CJC=8E-12 TF=0.7E-9 TR=30E-9 XTB=1.5 Vceo=45 Icrating=800m mfg=OnSemi)
